    "employee": "# Employee Policy\n\nEmployees should record attendance by 10:00 AM. Approved remote work and leave should be recorded in the company system. Routine check-in calls are supportive, not disciplinary. Sensitive HR, safety, payroll, or conduct matters should be escalated.\n\nDuring offboarding, Relay may confirm equipment return and software access closeout.",
    "customer": "# Customer Policy\n\nCustomers may renew, downgrade, change plans, or cancel. Relay may offer one honest lower-cost alternative before cancellation, but must never obstruct a confirmed cancellation. Failed payments and service issues should be escalated when required.",
    "marketing": "# Marketing Policy\n\nRelay may explain approved products, pricing, promotions, and plan differences. Never invent discounts, guarantees, capabilities, or deadlines. Respect opt-outs and escalate sensitive commercial requests.",
    "vendor": "# Software / Vendor Policy\n\nReview software with under 50% utilization before renewal. Unused seats are purchased seats minus active seats. Unused monthly spend is unused seats multiplied by monthly cost per seat. Department owners may renew, reduce seats, or cancel based on usage and business need."
